+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` validates incoming tool arguments against each registered tool's declared `inputSchema` before calling its executor, returning a descriptive rejection `ToolResponse` rather than throwing so the model can correct malformed calls within the existing tool-loop budget.
+
+## Validation Contract
+
+- Before running a tool executor, `ToolRegistry.execute` validates `input` against the resolved `inputSchema` for `required`, declared types, and `enum` constraints without coercing types, applying defaults, or rejecting unlisted properties when `additionalProperties` is unset, returning a `ToolResponse` naming the failing constraint when invalid ([validated by: rejects invalid input before calling the executor and keeps valid input unmodified](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L23)).
+- Registering a static `ToolDefinition` compiles its `inputSchema` once at `register` time and throws synchronously naming the tool when the schema cannot be compiled ([validated by: throws synchronously when registering a static tool with an invalid inputSchema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L74)).
+- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves its current `inputSchema` per `execute` call and validates against the resolved schema rather than a stale earlier version ([validated by: validates per call against the schema resolved from a dynamic ToolDefinitionSource](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L88)).
+- A static tool compiles its validator once at registration time rather than recompiling on subsequent `execute` calls.
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` throws `Unknown tool: <name>` only when no tool with that name is registered; schema validation failures return a `ToolResponse` instead of throwing.
+
+## Observability and Orchestration
+
+- Rejected tool inputs emit a warning log naming the tool and failing field constraint while omitting raw input values from both log records and returned `ToolResponse` text ([validated by: logs a warning on invalid input and omits raw input values from logs and rejection text](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L123)).
+- In `createChatOrchestrator`, a schema-rejected tool call returns its `ToolResponse.result` to the model as a `tool_result` without aborting the turn so a corrected follow-up call can succeed within `maxToolRounds` ([validated by: feeds a schema validation rejection back to the model so a corrected follow-up call succeeds](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L182)).
